{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Peter Prepares for Final Exams", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Accounting, What a Drag!", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 6, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 10, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Accurately use information about people's jobs and places of work in communicative situations", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.'", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Ask If/When People Are Free ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you want to spend time with someone, you ask them if or when they are free.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use these phrases to ask people if or when they are free:<br/><br/>Are you free on \u2026 ?<br/>How does (day) sound?<br/>When are you free to \u2026 ?<br/>What day are you free?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Are you free on Saturday? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "How does Sunday sound? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "When are you free to study for the exam? <br/> <br/> <br/>", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Modals Will, May, Might", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the modals <span class=\"italic\">may</span> and <span class=\"italic\">might</span> to show possibility. They have the same meaning.<br/>You use the modal <span class=\"italic\">will</span> to predict the future in a more certain way.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Modals go before a verb in the base form. The verb does not change.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I may take a futurology course next term. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I might be free if I finish the class project. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Technology will make our lives better. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We will have a world government.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "major", "type": "name"}, {"content": "in college or university, the subject of study of the majority of your courses", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm doing a major in humanities.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le10ob06aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about programs of study.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "minor", "type": "name"}, {"content": "in college or university, the subject of study of a few of your courses", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Accounting is only a minor for me.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le10ob06aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "subject", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a topic of study in a school (different courses can be the same subject)", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The humanities are subjects like literature and philosophy.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le10ob06aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "literature", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the study of works of writing, like books, plays, poems, etc.", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Do you like your course in English literature?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le10ob06aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "history", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the study of the past", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm very interested in world history.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le10ob06aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "the humanities", "type": "name"}, {"content": "subjects such as history, philosophy, literature, or religion", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My courses are in the humanities this term.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engen